INT. STAGE DOOR - GRAND MERIDIAN THEATRE - NIGHT

The backstage corridor of an old playhouse. Peeling posters, a cracked mirror, a radiator knocking like a dying heart. A single bulb in a wire cage swings gently. There is no draught.

The final performance has ended. Six members of the company stand in their street clothes, coats half-on, none of them going home.

AUGUSTINE BLACKWOOD (60s, director, silk scarf) stares at the stage door.

MIRABELLE TRUJILLO (30s, lead actress, make-up still on one eye) grips her handbag.

THADDEUS GRANT (40s, stage manager, headset around his neck) counts heads with his finger.

PRUDENCE WILKES-AMARI (20s, understudy, bright red coat) bites her thumbnail.

CORNELIUS FAIRCHILD (50s, prop master, apron) cradles a skull from the final scene.

BARTHOLOMEW "BARTY" NKEMELU (teen, call-boy, cap) hovers at the back.

THADDEUS
Five. I count five.

AUGUSTINE
Six, Thaddeus.

THADDEUS
Five and Barty.

MIRABELLE
Six, then.

PRUDENCE
Who's missing?

CORNELIUS
Nobody's missing.

BARTY
There was somebody in the wings. During the third act.

AUGUSTINE
That was the ghost light.

BARTY
It moved.

THADDEUS
Lights don't move.

PRUDENCE
It was a man.

MIRABELLE
It was Cornelius, getting the skull.

CORNELIUS
I was at the prop table.

A beat. The bulb swings. The shadow of the cage drifts slowly across their faces. Nobody looks up.

The radiator knocks twice. Then once.

AUGUSTINE
Whose coat is that?

On a hook by the stage door hangs a long black coat with a velvet collar. Nobody moves toward it.

MIRABELLE
(almost inaudible)
It wasn't there at the interval.

PRUDENCE
It's cold.

THADDEUS
Everyone, out. Now. Barty, the keys.

BARTY
I left them on the...

THADDEUS
Barty.

BARTY
I left them in the prompt corner.

Silence. Thaddeus turns. Down the corridor, the stage door to the auditorium is open a hand's width. Inside, in the dark, the ghost light burns, and in front of it, small and still, stands a figure with its back to them, face to the empty seats.

CORNELIUS
(whispering)
Don't look.

They all look.

The skull in Cornelius's arms clacks its jaw, softly, once. He drops it. It rolls under the radiator.

AUGUSTINE
(barely a breath)
Nobody run.

PRUDENCE
Nobody...

MIRABELLE
Yes.

THADDEUS
Run.

They run.

FADE OUT.
